    {
      "id": "fojxrwl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Foundation of the Mughal Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The chapter outlines the Foundation of the Mughal Empire and its progression.",
        "Prominent early rulers covered include Babur (1526–1530), Humayun, and Akbar the Great.",
        "Core administrative structure is detailed under Mughal Administration.",
        "Cultural aspects and construction are captured in Mughal Art and Architecture.",
        "The sequence concludes with the Decline of the Mughal Empire and SSC Exam Important Facts."
      ],
      "id": "tjifusl"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p1kx6b2",
      "content": "• Babur, a descendant of Timur and Genghis Khan, founded the Mughal Empire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qx7klkz",
      "content": "• He defeated Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat in 1526."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "irzblvq",
      "content": "• The victory marked the beginning of Mughal rule in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txi6lt6",
      "content": "• Babur also fought important battles like the Battle of Khanwa (1527) against Rana Sanga."
    },
    {
      "id": "aipllea",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Important Mughal Rulers"
    },
    {
