            "<p>Supreme authority of the empire</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mansabdari System</p>",
            "<p>Ranking system for officials and soldiers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Suba</p>",
            "<p>Province of the empire</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Subedar</p>",
            "<p>Governor of province</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Jagirdari System</p>",
            "<p>Land revenue assignment system</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8g4yz8x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Jahangir"
    },
    {
      "id": "j4ozr3e",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "iq7c1q2",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Cluster_013_GS & GK GUIDE BOOK/images/image_iq7c1q2.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cgselt3",
      "content": "<img></img>• Son of Akbar."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9wanmv8",
      "content": "• Known for the chain of justice (Zanjir-i-Adl)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hp8eqmu",
      "content": "• British ambassador Sir Thomas Roe visited his court."
    },
    {
      "id": "2jwgkfu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Shah Jahan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k0fzgwx",
      "content": "• Period known for architectural achievements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "03k6iz7",
      "content": "• Built the Taj Mahal in memory of Mumtaz Mahal."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gwpurue",
      "content": "• Also built Red Fort and Jama Masjid in Delhi."
    },
    {
      "id": "36oipvg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Aurangzeb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iojag4a",
      "content": "• Last powerful Mughal ruler."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8eejyrd",
      "content": "• Expanded Mughal territory to its maximum extent."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "foeccya",
      "content": "• Reimposed the Jizya tax on non-Muslims."
    },
    {
      "id": "kkmzyuh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Mughal Art and Architecture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m4293om",
      "content": "• Taj Mahal is one of the Seven Wonders of the World."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tjbm9fm",
      "content": "• Red Fort in Delhi was built by Shah Jahan."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vpuv0s4",
      "content": "• Mughal architecture combines Persian, Indian and Islamic styles."
    },
    {
      "id": "b5dnekn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. Decline of the Mughal Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "52j8xa7",
      "content": "• Weak successors after Aurangzeb."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chronological sequence and dates of major rulers, starting with Babur (1526–1530).",
        "Administrative reforms introduced during the reign of Akbar the Great.",
        "Artistic and architectural monuments created during the Mughal period.",
        "Key historical reasons behind the Decline of the Mughal Empire."
      ],
      "id": "ionyqdk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r9pdbhf",
      "content": "• Rise of regional powers such as Marathas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e3y3dr0",
      "content": "• Foreign invasions by Nadir Shah and Ahmad Shah Abdali."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mvj6dx4",
      "content": "• British expansion weakened Mughal authority."
    },
    {
      "id": "ehdk1al",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC Exam Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y9i5w4h",
      "content": "• Mughal Empire founded in 1526 by Babur."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ce1vd7w",
      "content": "• Akbar introduced the Mansabdari system."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3vklr5t",
      "content": "• Taj Mahal was built by Shah Jahan."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bdby5ap",
      "content": "• Sir Thomas Roe visited Jahangir's court."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0z2zcbi",
      "content": "• Aurangzeb was the last powerful Mughal ruler."
    }
  ],
